Task Manager API
================

A small task management API built with Symfony, following a layered / clean architecture approach.

------------------------------------------------------------

Requirements
------------
- PHP 8.2+
- Composer
- Symfony CLI (optional, for local server)
- SQLite (used by default)

------------------------------------------------------------

Installation
------------

1. Clone the repository

   git clone https://github.com/Auke-Loosman/task-manager
   cd task-manager

2. Install dependencies

   composer install

3. Environment configuration

   Copy the example environment file:

   cp .env.local.example .env.local

   The project uses SQLite by default. The database file will be created automatically in:

   var/data.db

4. Create the database schema

   php bin/console doctrine:schema:create

5. Start the application

   Using Symfony CLI:

   symfony serve

   Or using PHP built-in server:

   php -S 127.0.0.1:8000 -t public

------------------------------------------------------------

Running Tests
-------------

The project contains unit, integration, and functional tests.

To run all tests:

   php bin/phpunit

Tests use a separate test environment and database configuration.

------------------------------------------------------------

API Endpoints
-------------

- POST /tasks
  Create a new task

- GET /tasks
  List all tasks

- GET /tasks/{id}
  Fetch a task by ID

- PATCH /tasks/{id}/status
  Update task status (todo → in_progress → done)

- DELETE /tasks/{id}
  Delete a task (not allowed when status is done)

------------------------------------------------------------

Architecture
------------

The project is structured using a clean architecture approach:

- Domain
  Contains business rules, entities, value objects, and domain logic.

- Application
  Contains use cases implemented as commands, queries, and handlers.

- Infrastructure
  Contains technical details such as Doctrine persistence and repositories.

- Presentation
  Contains HTTP controllers, request DTOs, and response mapping.

Symfony Messenger is used to dispatch commands and queries to their respective handlers.

------------------------------------------------------------

Manual Testing
--------------

In addition to automated tests, the API was manually tested using Postman.

Requests were sent for:
- Creating tasks
- Listing tasks
- Fetching tasks by ID
- Updating task status
- Deleting tasks

This was used to verify correct HTTP responses and state transitions alongside the test suite.

------------------------------------------------------------
